## Legibility and look
- **Title / play / game over are visually consistent**: same dark blue-grey, same green accent (logo, snake, buttons, score digits), red for Game Over; same wall frame around all three (`01-title.png`, `06-play-score3.png`, `07-gameover-run1-self.png`).
- **Walls** (new brick ring) read clearly against the dark board; the field edge is unmistakable. Wall death occurs when the head would enter the ring; the head is never drawn inside it.
- **Food** (red apple with yellow stalk) stands out from board and snake and is not confused with anything.
- **Head** has eyes and a slightly lighter green; it reads as the head, including when the snake is 29 cells long (`evidence/pt3/10-long-snake-1.png`). **Tail** tip is pointed and visible.
- **Corners (minor):** at a turn the body segment is drawn as a short stub with a visible seam/notch (screenshot 10-long-snake-1 near x≈770,y≈440); it looks slightly lumpy/disconnected but stays readable and never ambiguous about where the snake goes.
- **Body vs head colour (minor):** head and body are nearly the same green; the eyes carry the distinction. Fine at this size.
- Game-over screen dims the snake and food under a dark overlay; the final score and button are easy to read.

## Sound
- All 4 sounds load (`SnakeAssets.status` lists `.ogg` for start, eat, gameover, music). Observed by hooking `play()`: `start.ogg` at game start, `music.ogg` (looping) right after, `eat.ogg` **exactly once per food** (36 plays for score 36), `gameover.ogg` on death; music pauses on pause, blur and game over, and resumes on resume.
- **M mutes**: with sound off no `play()` calls fire and music stays paused; unmuting restarts music.
- **I could not hear the sounds**: headless Chromium has no audio output and the `audio-understanding` resource returned HTTP 429 (daily request limit of 20 reached on the shared key), so no listening verdict from it. Objective analysis of the `.wav` files instead: start 0.32 s (peak 0.80, dominant 784 Hz), eat 0.13 s (992 Hz), gameover 0.85 s (209 Hz), music 4.8 s loop (175 Hz); none clips, none has leading/trailing clicks except one note below; lengths fit `docs/assets.md`. Whether they are *pleasant* and in sync with events is **not verified by listening**: someone with audio output (or the audio resource once its limit resets) should check. In sync by construction: each sound is triggered in the same step that causes it.
- **Minor, music loop seam:** first sample amplitude 0.125 vs last 0.018, so the 4.8 s loop may click at the repeat; and 4.8 s is short, so the repetition will be noticeable in a long run.

## Problems and friction (all minor)
1. 3rd key within a single tick is dropped (queue of 2).
2. Corner segments show a small seam.
3. Music loop is 4.8 s with a possible click at the seam.
4. Game-over input guard (game-developer#4) is **not in this build**: Game Over still accepts Enter/Space immediately. Will re-check when it lands.

